{
  "about": "The board-reference language (.kicad_pcb, .kicad_sch), asserted by packages/core/src/lib/boardRefs.js and cadgen/kicad/refs.py alike. A part is its reference designator (a letter or '_', then letters, digits, '_', '+' or '-': what KiCad boards and board.part(ref=...) use), a pad or pin follows a dot, a net is net:<name> (JSON-quoted when the name holds whitespace, a quote, a comma, '@' or '#'), and a point is @x<x>y<y> in the script's millimetres (y up): comma-free, because a token joins several selectors with commas, as STEP tokens do (split outside quotes); whitespace inside a quoted name is the name's, anywhere else it ends the token. Canonical points drop trailing zeros and a negative zero.",
